 least help keep things moving, Iam in the process of rewriting large chunks of the lib. I have rewritten all wiz commands, and will start on the player commands (and the help    files) soon. Uglymouth has been working on the man pages, but he has beeninactive lately, so I might take over that as well. I am also rewriting  all of the main inheritable files, hopefully making them easier to use andunderstand, and allowing more people who don't know (and don't want toknow) alot of LPC to contribute and create imaginative areas.Kryll has been working on a totally new guild system which will allowmulti-guilding with specialization. I know he's not been around much recently, but he lost his job, moved to a new state, got a new job, gotmarried... so I think we can give him some slack. :) This will hopefullyrevitalize things further and make playing fun again. He and I are also  working on rewriting the living/player code to make everything worktogether. This includes rewriting things like combat (including thearmour/weapon code), races and religion.What I would love to do is get all the wizards to work with the newinheritables (once I finish them) and create brand new areas/quests withthe ultimate aim of scrapping the existing world alltogether andeffectively making a new HM. However this will take alot of time andco-operation from people, and right now that doesn't seem to beforthcoming. What I might try and instigate is a new continent... we can leave the existing one 'as is' (just fixing bugs) and start work on a    brand new location. Players could choose to log in to either the old or  the new continents, and there would be transportation between the two    (boats and dragon airways spring to mind as two existing options). This   new continent would be more spread out and it's geography would be plannedso that areas of vastly differing location types aren't placed next toeach other. You can type 'map' on HM for one such plan that I wrote lastyear. My virtual area code will allow us to easily create 'filler' areasto pad out the map until we have enough areas to do the job.The above has focused mainly on what is wrong here from a code point of view. I know that the lack of players doesn't help motivate the coders tocontinue, but I firmly believe in three points:1. There is no point atracting in new players until we fix up the code of   the mud... All that will happen is that we will lose the new players   again (they may be PKed alot, or they may sense the frustration and   futility from the wizards or whatever...) and then it will be doubly    hard to get more new players if we ever do fix up the mud.   2. If we do not fix up this mud's code, it will die. There are too many   good new muds out there, let alone all the graphical online games that   are springing up, for a 6 year old 2.4.5 mud to survive without radical   changes.3. We are all here to have fun - players and wizards alike. If it ceases     to be fun, then maybe it is time to move on.My suggestion would be to spend as much time as you feel you want tohere... I would like to think that you could help me with some of the   above, along with John (Texas) and Simon (Dworkin), and people likeKryll, Mangla and Warlord who want to turn this mud around again. However,if RL seems more appealing, then go for it. :) I only code consistently ontwo muds these days... I don't have the enthusiasm or loyalty to code formore (I've tried). The other mud I code for is still in alpha phase, so ithas no players at all - even more boring. :)If you really want to move to another mud, I can point you in thedirection of one that I code for occasionally, but I would much prefer itif you helped me get this place moving again.   Hope to talk to you soon.Dave**montoya**To: demolianSubj: Contact Email AddressCc: sauron, daniella, darastor, jewelDate: Apr 26Yo Guys and Girls.... this message is going out to quite a few of 