e to be his mentor (stop laughing!).  What exactly isthe process?  Does he ask one of you arch-types to promote him to apprenticefirst, or does he ask me to ask you?  I never had a mentor...  I think youbanished him or something :)Anyway, he says he can code, and he's on quite a bit, and I've never heard ofhim being a problem...**mangla**To: wilbieRe:   MentorsCc: archesDate: Sep 12Being a mentor means you agree to support and helphim when he is learning to code. If you agree to be his mentorthen you will set the mentor quest to him. this tells thearches that you are prepared to stand behind him and pushhim over the cli...err push him in the right direction.Before you set the mentor quest, review his qualifictionsas far as wizzing goes. Does he have the percentage to wiz?Does he have the XP needed? Is he old enough?Then he will have ot ask the aches for permission to wiz.We will set the ask_god quest to him and then he willbe able to go to his guild and advance wiz.That about sum it up?-Mangla**wilbie**To: manglaSubj: SmorlokCc: sauron, haplo, airborneDate: Sep 12He's got the age, and at Legend 20 I think he's got the experience.  Most importantly (to me anyway) he seems like he wants to code some cool areasand help out the mud.  So I did the mentor thing.He's coded on HM2 (don't hold that against him - a lot of us did) and he sayshe has coded on others as well.  I am planning to be here quite a bit more,unless things at work get really screwed - we're replacing a mainframewith an SAP/WinNT network and it's deadlined at November 2nd :)Anyway, I will help him as much as a I can, and HM has always been easy to get a handle on.  I think he'll make a great wizard.Wilbie**mangla**To: sauronSubj: updated rwhere dataDate: Oct  4Added my new IP and removed my old on.-Mangla**tats**To: sauronSubj: IPDate: Oct  6My rwhere should read Washington, North Carolina**redsexy**To: sauronSubj: Remind me.