ore potent.  I think if we do things like this that we should perhaps balance meditation skillswith something like 'can only meditate in a temple'... with that being just one example.W.**airborne**To: sauronSubj: healing...Cc: archesDate: Nov  1Sorry about that, zigged when I should have zagged.Here's the idea that I have been bouncing about in my head.  Ok, suppose we limit meditation/healing skills to only the guild roomand \"shrines\".  Then we give guild members the ability to create shrines in various locations.  Players will be able to have their healing, but they would have to work a bit for it.  To start, we'd have the shrine needed to be built.  An easy way toget players to spend a bunch of gold on all sorts of things, bowls, statues, insense, etc.  Then they would have to protect those locationsonce they were built.  Certainly leaving lots of valuables laying around would tempt almost any player, which would kinda be the point.Add in the idea that some elements of theshrine would degrade withtime (insence comes to mind) and have to be replaced every so often.  The idea is to create an economy by finding reasons for players to gatheror purchase things that aren't just for killing.  If insence were onlyavailable in a small handful of locations, and there was a demand for itwe'd create the demand.  It helps control healing rates, keeps moneydown a bit, adds a roleplaying element to the mud, and encourages guildsto work together.Ideas and critics?**eponine**To: sauronSubj: heyDate: Nov  5how do you remove an engagement ring around here?-catherine**tatsuo**To: manglaSubj: ideasCc: airborne, sauronDate: Nov  6My ideas, or shit that i just am not current on.I went throught the wizards directory and fingered every wiz.1/10 shows more than bi monthly log in50% are gone, no biggy90% appear to have done nothing newThe GM's are lacking in ability, missing, or just changing values set by the peoplew